A||||4||Jncomutt||84 Shifting rough, notchy||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||12-14-2001||07:43 PM||||I've noticed that my 84 shifts much more difficult and like notchy than anyother car I've driven.  I'm not sure if thats just how fieros are or not.  We have an 89 CRX Si, and it shifts effortlessly.  Same thing with our beretta, push the clutch, and you can move it with a pinky finger...<P>My Fiero on the other hand, Requires a good tug on the shifter to get it where its got to go.  Also, it doesnt' feel like smooth changes, kinda notchy...<P>I have new master and slave cyliders, new steel pedal, and clutch was replaced 5k ago...  So I know thats all in good working order...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||12-14-2001||08:55 PM||||The shifter on the 84's contributes to the hard/notchy feeling. It is a little shorter than the 85+ and makes for less mechanical advantage over the cables/shift mechanism. My car has a tranny from an 84 with a modified (quick throw) shifter, new cables, clutch, and master/slave cylinders. It is very tough to shift when compared to my Civic, but about the same as other Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||12-14-2001||08:59 PM||||OK.. thanks Cooter, thats what I was lookin for.  I have a short throw on mine too, guess that contributes to it.  Those Civics are easy, for those girls ta drive... =)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-14-2001||09:24 PM||||No problem- I used to have a CRX too. An '88 Si. Not enough room so I sold it and ended up with a '90 3 door Si.||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||12-14-2001||09:43 PM||||My wife won't drive my Fiero as it is hard to shift.  I don't see this as a bad thing.  I'd try bleeding the the system using Archie's  bleeding method.  I did that plus changed to Valvoline syntheic Brake fluid and Mobil 1 in the tranny, which helped smooth it out quite a bit.  Don't know which helped the most as I did all three at the same time.  ||||reg||1
